{
  "title": "Filter out Serious Eats guide articles (Article schema, no Recipe) \
from the recipe pipeline",
  "description": "Some Serious Eats URLs in `data/test-urls.json` are \
editorial guides rather than recipes — for example \
`https://www.seriouseats.com/food-lab-complete-guide-to-sous-vide-steak`. The \
page's only JSON-LD entry is `@type: Article`, with no embedded Recipe schema \
and no `structured-ingredients` or `structured-project__steps` markup, so even \
the HTML fallback added in #485 (split-out p3 issue) cannot recover a recipe — \
there is no recipe in the body to extract.\n\
\n\
Today these guide URLs fail `extract_recipe` with `Missing required field` and \
silently drop out of snapshot generation. They were probably scraped into the \
Paprika export by mistake (a user clipped a guide instead of a recipe).\n\
\n\
Fix shape:\n\
\n\
  - decide where to filter. Either drop guide-style URLs at \
`generate_test_urls`/`refilter-test-urls` time (heuristic on URL slug, e.g. \
`/food-lab-complete-guide-`, `/food-lab-`, or detect Article-only schema \
during the fetch step), or surface them as a distinct, expected \
snapshot-skipped category instead of a hard error.\n\
  - audit `data/test-urls.json` for similar guide URLs and drop or annotate \
them.\n\
  - document the chosen approach in `doc/` so the next time someone wonders \
why a Serious Eats URL doesn't produce a snapshot they have a clear answer.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "pipeline",
    "extraction",
  ],
